    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nCython crashes in `ConstantFolding` when a comprehension whose loop target contains a starred name (`*_`) appears as the right-hand side of an **augmented** assignment (`+=`, `|=`).\n\n`Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py:visit_SequenceNode` assumes every arg has a `.target` attribute, but a starred target yields a `NameNode`, which does not.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour\n\n```python\n# a.py — valid, working Python; f([('a', 1, 'x'), ('b', 2)]) == [1, 2]\ndef f(xs):\n    out = []\n    out += [c for k, c, *_ in xs]\n    return out\n```\n\n```console\n$ cythonize -3 a.py\n```\n\nWhat matters is the **augmented** assignment; a plain `+` compiles fine:\n\n| variant | result |\n|---|---|\n| `out += [c for k, c, *_ in xs]` | **crash** |\n| `out += [x for x, *_ in xs]` | **crash** |\n| `out \\|= {x for x, *_ in xs}` (set comp) | **crash** |\n| `out = [c for k, c in p] + [c for k, c, *_ in t]` (plain `+`) | ok |\n| `out = [c for k, c, *_ in xs]` (no augmented assignment) | ok |\n| `out += list(c for k, c, *_ in xs)` (genexp through `list()`) | ok |\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nCompiles, like the plain-`+` and plain-assignment forms do.\n\n### OS\n\nmacOS 15 (Darwin 25.4.0) and Debian (`python:3.12` Docker image) — both reproduce.\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.13, 3.14\n\n### Cython version\n\n**Every version tested crashes**, spanning three major releases:\n\n| Cython | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 0.29.37 | crash |\n| 3.0.0, 3.0.12 | crash |\n| 3.1.0, 3.1.4, 3.1.8 | crash |\n| 3.2.0, 3.2.4, 3.2.8, 3.2.9 | crash |\n| 3.3.0a1 | crash |\n\n### Additional context\n\nVerbatim output on 3.2.9 / CPython 3.12.13:\n\n```\nError compiling Cython file:\n------------------------------------------------------------\n...\ndef f(xs):\n    out = []\n    out += [c for k, c, *_ in xs]\n                  ^\n------------------------------------------------------------\na.py:3:18: Compiler crash in ConstantFolding\n\nAddNode.operand2 = ComprehensionNode(a.py:3:11,\n    has_local_scope = True,\n    is_temp = True,\n    result_is_used = True,\n    use_managed_ref = True)\nComprehensionNode.loop = ForInStatNode(a.py:3:14)\nForInStatNode.target = TupleNode(a.py:3:18,\n    is_sequence_constructor = 1,\n    result_is_used = True,\n    starred_assignment = True,\n    use_managed_ref = True)\n\nCompiler crash traceback from this point on:\n  File \"Cython/Compiler/Visitor.py\", line 174, in Cython.Compiler.Visitor.TreeVisitor._visit\n  File \".../Cython/Compiler/Optimize.py\", line 4822, in visit_SequenceNode\n    elif arg.target.is_sequence_constructor and not arg.target.mult_factor:\n         ^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'NameNode' object has no attribute 'target'\n```\n\nThis surfaced in a real codebase where the module runs fine as pure Python — the crash only appears when the file is compiled with Cython, so a green test suite gives no warning.\n\n*(Edited: the original report claimed a preceding non-starred comprehension was needed to trigger this. It is not — a single starred comprehension on the RHS of an augmented assignment is enough. The MRE and the variant table above are corrected accordingly.)*\n",
